147	118,469,590,1353	147. Spadix and Spathe.	The hood-like spathe of Indian-Turnip, striped and shaded, with its front cut away to show the spadix inside, club-shaped above and crowded with small flowers near the bottom.
148	773,1517,1320,1893	148. Compound Umbel.	A compound umbel of Caraway: rays spreading from the top of one stalk, each ending in a little umbellet of small flowers and buds.
149	1415,1047,1725,2117	149. Panicle.	A simple panicle: a tall stalk with side branches, each once branched and carrying round buds and open, nodding flowers.
